  "question": {
    "text": "Let $f$ be a composite function of $x$ defined by $f(u)=\\frac{1}{u^2+u-2}, u(x)=\\frac{1}{x-1}$.\nThen the number of points $x$ where $f$ is discontinuous is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "RPiGz",
      "text": "\n4\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SzVnR",
      "text": "\n3\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "eIUnT",
      "text": "\n2\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "aHyPl",
      "text": "\n1",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mu(x)=\\frac{1}{x-1}$, which is discontinous at $x=1$\n$$\nf(u)=\\frac{1}{u^2+u-2}=\\frac{1}{(u+2)(u-1)},\n$$\nwhich is discontinous at $u=-2,1$\nwhen $u=-2$, then $\\frac{1}{x-1}=-2 \\Rightarrow x=\\frac{1}{2}$\nwhen $u=1$, then $\\frac{1}{x-1}=1 \\Rightarrow x=2$\nHence given composite function is discontinous at three points, $x=1, \\frac{1}{2}$ and 2 .",
    "image": null
